  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Justice obligated $775M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Justice recorded 6,926 awards with an average award size of $112K. Obligations fell 92.7% year over year. Fiscal-year totals from prior years show FY22 at $9B, FY23 at $10B, FY24 at $9.4B, FY25 at $8.6B, and FY26 at $10.5B. The FY2027 to date portfolio is concentrated in security and health services: Security Guards and Patrol Services accounts for $182M and General Medical and Surgical Hospitals accounts for $94.1M. The top vendors reflect that mix: METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. received $123M and SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION received $33.1M. The FY2027 to date totals are partial, fiscal year to date, and represent contract obligations for the current fiscal year period only. Agencies and contractors should note the shift in scale from prior full fiscal years to the FY2027 to date figure of $775M when comparing activity or planning engagements.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations fall so sharply in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Justice obligated $775M in FY2027 to date, and obligations fell 92.7% year over year. Prior full fiscal years ranged from $8.6B to $10.5B, so the FY2027 to date total is much smaller than those annual totals. The FY2027 to date figure is partial, fiscal year to date, which explains part of the difference when comparing to full-year obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is Justice spending its FY2027 to date contracting dollars?",
        "body": "Security Guards and Patrol Services is the largest category with $182M and General Medical and Surgical Hospitals is the second with $94.1M. Other notable categories include Other Computer Related Services at $75M and All Other Legal Services at $40.1M. METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. is the top vendor with $123M and several health and services vendors appear in the top ten list."
      }
    ]
  },
